Subject: [PATCH 4/5] fix(i18n): coded diagnoses in the summary use the UI
 language

The tooltip and the whole-mouth summary printed every coded diagnosis with
its WHO ICD-10 title, in English, in every language. Outside English they now
use the language's dx.<key> name (already used by the active-diagnoses card)
next to the same ICD-10 code. English keeps the DX-8 refined WHO titles; the
FHIR export still carries the WHO titles.

Tests: dx-summary-language.test.ts (en, fr, ar, hu, whole-mouth summary).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
